; printer_notes = QIDI i-Fast (2021, legacy Chitu/Marlin generation) - community profile.\nDerived from OrcaSlicer's stock 'Qidi X-Max 0.4 nozzle' (AGPL-3.0; upstream Bambu Studio / PrusaSlicer). Geometry and dual-extruder configuration from QIDI's published reference/qidi-profiles/prusaslicer/PrusaSlicer_fast.ini; start, end and tool-change G-code from QIDI Print reference exports (see reference/extracted-gcode.md).\nNetwork printing is intentionally unconfigured: the i-Fast uses a proprietary UDP protocol OrcaSlicer does not support. Extruder offsets are handled in firmware and MUST stay zero here. Head auto-lift on tool change is firmware behaviour.\nSee TODO.md for every value still needing verification on the machine.
